better112.option.distortion_effects=Distortion Effects
better112.option.distortion_effects.tooltip=How strongly the screen wobbles from nausea and from standing in a Nether portal.
better112.option.menu_blur=Menu Background Blur
better112.option.menu_blur.tooltip=Blurs the world behind menus and inventories, as Minecraft 1.21 does. Not used while another mod's screen effect is showing.
better112.option.keybind_search=Controls Search
better112.option.keybind_search.tooltip=Adds a search box and a filter to the Controls screen. Search by name or category, or type @ and a key (@R) to list everything set to that key. The filter shows only clashing, unbound or changed keys.
better112.option.equipment_compare=Equipment Comparison
better112.option.equipment_compare.tooltip=The tooltip of armor, a weapon or a tool is joined by the tooltip of what you wear or hold in its place.
better112.option.durability_warning=Low Durability Warning
better112.option.durability_warning.tooltip=A sound and a message above the hotbar when a held tool or worn armor drops to a tenth of its durability, and again just before it breaks.
better112.option.death_coords=Death Coordinates
better112.option.death_coords.tooltip=Shows where you died on the death screen, and puts it in chat, where a click fills in a teleport command.
better112.option.glint_speed=Glint Speed
better112.option.glint_speed.tooltip=How fast the shimmer on enchanted items and armor moves, as in Minecraft 1.19. 100% is the usual speed.
better112.option.glint_strength=Glint Strength
better112.option.glint_strength.tooltip=How bright the shimmer on enchanted items and armor is, as in Minecraft 1.19.
better112.option.freelook=Freelook
better112.option.freelook.tooltip=While the Freelook key (F4 unless changed in Controls) is held, the mouse swings the camera around you in third person; you keep walking and aiming the way you faced.
better112.option.zoom_scroll=Scroll to Zoom
better112.option.zoom_scroll.tooltip=While the Zoom key is held, the mouse wheel zooms further in or out instead of changing the held item, and the zoom eases in and out.
better112.option.new_item_marks=New Item Marks
better112.option.new_item_marks.tooltip=Items you pick up get a small star in inventory screens until the mouse passes over them.
better112.option.world_search=World Search
better112.option.world_search.tooltip=A search box on the Select World screen, as in Minecraft 1.16. Right click it to clear it.
better112.option.chat_timestamps=Chat Timestamps
better112.option.chat_timestamps.tooltip=The time each chat message arrived, in front of it. Hover it for the date.
better112.option.chat_copy=Copy and Keep Chat
better112.option.chat_copy.tooltip=Right click a chat message to copy it. A message closed unsent with Escape is still there the next time the chat opens.
better112.option.biome_titles=Arrival Titles
better112.option.biome_titles.tooltip=The name of a dimension when you arrive in it, and of a biome once you have walked into it, fades in above the middle of the screen, as the Traveler's Titles mod shows them.
better112.option.skip_front_view=Skip Front View
better112.option.skip_front_view.tooltip=The perspective key (F5) goes from first person to the view from behind and straight back, leaving out the view of your own face.
better112.option.clear_lava_fog=Clearer Lava with Fire Resistance
better112.option.clear_lava_fog.tooltip=With Fire Resistance, or in spectator mode, you can see a few blocks into lava instead of under one, as since Minecraft 1.17.
better112.option.background_volume=Background Volume
better112.option.background_volume.tooltip=How loud the game is while its window is in the background, as the Dynamic FPS mod does it. At Unchanged the game sounds the same either way.
better112.option.better_grass=Better Grass
better112.option.better_grass.tooltip=Grass, mycelium and podzol are drawn green down their sides where the slope carries on downward, so hillsides read as one surface, as OptiFine's Better Grass does. Fast does it on every side.
better112.option.falling_leaves=Falling Leaves
better112.option.falling_leaves.tooltip=Leaves drift down from the trees, in each tree's own colour, as the Falling Leaves mod (and Minecraft 1.20's cherry trees) show them. Off when particles are set to minimal.
better112.option.fireflies=Fireflies
better112.option.fireflies.tooltip=Small glowing lights drift over grass and plants on warm, dry nights in forests, swamps, plains and jungles, as with Minecraft 1.21.5's firefly bushes. Off when particles are set to minimal.
better112.option.jei_search_highlight=JEI Search in Inventories
better112.option.jei_search_highlight.tooltip=While JEI's search box has the keyboard, items in the open inventory that the search does not match are dimmed and the ones it does are outlined, as EMI and REI do. JEI's own search syntax works (@mod, #tooltip, $ore).
better112.option.rarity_borders=Rarity Borders
better112.option.rarity_borders.tooltip=Uncommon, rare and epic items, and items a mod names in a colour, get a thin frame of that colour in slots and on the hotbar, and a tooltip border to match.
better112.option.clearer_water=Clearer Water
better112.option.clearer_water.tooltip=Seeing under water gets better the longer you stay under, up to a good distance, as since Minecraft 1.13. Respiration and Water Breathing still help.
better112.option.debug_targets=More F3 Lines
better112.option.debug_targets.tooltip=The F3 screen also shows the ore names of the block you look at, and names the fluid (as since 1.13) and the entity (as since 1.14) you look at.
better112.option.item_zoom=Item Zoom
better112.option.item_zoom.tooltip=In an inventory or JEI, the Item Zoom key (Z unless changed in Controls) switches on a large picture of the item under the mouse beside the screen, as the Item Zoom mod does. Press it again to switch it off.
better112.option.better_mount_hud=Better Mount HUD
better112.option.better_mount_hud.tooltip=Riding keeps your own food bar on screen, with the mount's hearts above it, and a horse's jump bar only replaces the experience bar while a jump is charging, as the Better Mount HUD mod does.
better112.option.hide_own_effect_particles=Hide Own Effect Swirls
better112.option.hide_own_effect_particles.tooltip=In first person, the swirls of your own potion and beacon effects are not drawn, so they no longer float in front of your eyes. Others still see them, and so do you in third person.
better112.option.rain_ripples=Rain Ripples
better112.option.rain_ripples.tooltip=Rain makes small rings spread on open water, as the Effective and Particle Rain mods show it.
better112.option.idle_fps=Idle Frame Cap
better112.option.idle_fps.tooltip=Once nothing has been pressed or moved for five minutes, the game draws at most this many frames a second, as Dynamic FPS does. Machines and the world keep running at full speed; any key or mouse movement brings the frame rate back.
better112.debug.help.f4=F3 + F4 = Choose a game mode
better112.debug.help.c=F3 + C = Copy where you stand as a /tp command
better112.debug.help.i=F3 + I = Copy the block or entity you look at as a command
better112.controls.search=Search, or @key
better112.controls.none=No keys match
better112.worlds.search=Search...
better112.worlds.none=No worlds match
better112.chat.copied=Message copied
